---
desription: "Code quality and best practice rules"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Reduce duplicate code
Always try to avoid duplicating code. Always check to see if we already have a function, struct, error, event, etc. in the codebase already that you should use, instead of reimplementing it. If you touch multiple files, always check to make sure you didn't unecessarily duplicate code.

# Styling
After you apply changes, always check to make sure you're following our styleguide, located in @STYLEGUIDE.md. If you're breaking any rules in the styleguide, update your implementation to follow the style guide.

# Check linter and static analysis
After you apply changes and made sure you followed the styleguide, run `make check`. This command runs our automatic format, linters, slither static analysis, and test suite. 

Fix any warnings you see.

# Always ask clarifying questions when in doubt
If you ever have clarifying questions, always ask me.

